# Shared EA feature sets this board pulls in. One word per feature, space
# separated. Each lives in board/ea/common/features/<name>/, holding both its
# halves: defconfig (userspace) and linux.fragment (kernel).
#   wifi  - Atheros ath9k radio + wpa_supplicant/iw userspace
#   emmc  - sdhci-pci + ext4, persistent rootfs on mmcblk0p1
#   switch - BCM53125 managed switch over SPI (DSA/b53); gives lan1/lan2
#   audio  - CE5300 I2S + ADAU1451 codec, ALSA, AirPlay (shairport-sync)
#            and Spotify Connect (librespot)
wifi emmc switch audio

# RE-ENABLED (was `wifi emmc` while Home Assistant was brought up). This is the
# full EA-3 v1 feature set: it has the radio, the BCM53125 switch and the EA-3
# audio hardware.
#
# !!! SIZE: `switch` and `audio` are written =y in their feature fragments, and
# an x86_64 EA-3 kernel already fills ~7,037,952 of CEFDK's 7,417,856-byte
# bootlinux window (see git history / the old TEMPORARILY-DISABLED.md). =y
# switch+audio very likely OVERRUNS it, and an oversized bzImage is TRUNCATED
# silently and does not boot. The documented fix is to carry them as MODULES
# (=m) on the p1 rootfs — NOT done here because the switch's SPI/b53 drivers and
# the ASoC drivers are injected obj-y via board/ea/common/kernel/objs.mk and the
# switch board glue is built-in, so =m needs load-ordering + build/boot proof
# that cannot be done without a build. MEASURE the bzImage before trusting a boot.
# `audio` additionally has never been built for x86_64 (compile risk) and its
# platform driver is probe-only (enable_pcm=0; reading TX reg 0x2004 hangs the SoC).
#
# `wifi` stays affordable only because its fragment builds ath9k/mac80211/cfg80211
# as MODULES; as =y they were ~1 MB and did not fit either.
